These source packages aren't part of the AO tool and are provided for
test and demo purposes only.

The 'hello' directory contains a typical "Hello World" program. This is
the simplest demo and should generally be tried first. It's provided with
both a Makefile and a build.sh script for Unix build purposes. Any build
model may be used with AO; in fact that's the point of this demo.

Any other source packages here are simply downloaded open-source tools
known to work well with AO. They should be unpacked and built in the
standard, documented manner and then built with AO. Generally these
can be built on Unix via "sh configure && make clean all".
